<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">King of Bohemia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a> was the ruler of the Kingdom of Bohemia, a constituent realm of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a> centred on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prague">Prague</a>. Under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-bull-of-1356">Golden Bull of 1356</a> the King of Bohemia was one of the seven prince-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-elector">electors</a> who chose the emperor. The crown later passed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a>, tying Bohemia closely to imperial politics.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/king-of-bohemia.jpg" alt="King of Bohemia" width="320" height="379" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hugo Gerard Ströhl · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Znak_%C4%8Desk%C3%A9ho_kr%C3%A1lovstv%C3%AD.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
